                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] Experienced on the Oculus Rift with Touch Controllers [/h1]\n\nI got this game free as part of the Steam Curator program. That does not impact my review. However, what does impact my review is the difficulty. I was unable to unlock the 3rd room and thus could not progress to the other rooms. So my review is incomplete at best.\n\nThe good thing is that there are lots of puzzles to solve. The first door puzzle is very easy. It makes you think that everything else will be as well. Then you get to the second door puzzle and it is very obtuse. I was finally able to figure it out, but only after trying everything else. I would say it was obtuse but I've seen these types of answers before in several other puzzle games so maybe not that obtuse.\n\nThe third room I just can't figure out. I played an hour and just don't see what it wants. I think I have tried everything. I think I'm close to the answer. I just don't know what's holding it back.\n\nAnyways, the graphics are not that great. Sounds are meh. Movement is by teleportation and there is no snap or smooth turning. Grabbing objects seems clunky. I noticed you have to stand away from the object otherwise the object is bound to bounce off of you. You have different tools you can use from a gun (nerf gun?), to a torch, to a hammer, to light sabers, to shuriken. \n\nThere are 12 total rooms so normallly I would say you're getting a fair amount of content for the price, but in this case the production values are very low. I do recommend this game for puzzle fans though. And I would say it's a wait for sale. \n\nSale Price Rating 6/10. Normal Price Rating 5/10.",
